rvz_datasource: keep the partial word when padding starts inside one

The lagged-Fibonacci padding of an RVZ group skipped to the requested
offset through the word writer, which writes whole words: a read that
began inside a word started at the next word boundary instead, and the
bytes of the word it began in were lost (the patch's own comment). At the
pin c7ebd1b6e7 upstream's reader skips the same way.

The skip stops at the last whole word, the partial word is generated with
the output, and its leading bytes are dropped from what is returned.
Nothing else changes.

Written for ROCKNIX (fork issues pixelelated#583 and #584: RVZ through the
offline service, Dolphin routed to it), added in f9b7ce3dfb. No draft
under docs/upstream/raofflineproxy/ yet (a #585 line, T19 PL-19). Not sent
(D-WORKFLOW-165).

--- a/linux/raofflineproxy/rvz_datasource.py
+++ b/linux/raofflineproxy/rvz_datasource.py
@@ -663,12 +663,16 @@
 
     word_index = 0
     bytes_to_skip = absolute_offset % _SECTOR_SIZE
+    # Keep the partial word: skipping it through the word writer would
+    # round the requested byte offset up and discard its remaining bytes.
+    leading_bytes = bytes_to_skip % 4
+    bytes_to_skip -= leading_bytes
     if bytes_to_skip > 0:
         word_index = _write_lagged_fibonacci_bytes(buffer, bytearray(bytes_to_skip), bytes_to_skip, word_index)
 
-    output = bytearray(size)
-    _write_lagged_fibonacci_bytes(buffer, output, size, word_index)
-    return bytes(output)
+    output = bytearray(size + leading_bytes)
+    _write_lagged_fibonacci_bytes(buffer, output, len(output), word_index)
+    return bytes(memoryview(output)[leading_bytes:])
 
 
 def _write_lagged_fibonacci_bytes(buffer: list, output: bytearray, byte_count: int, initial_word_index: int) -> int:
